## Why This Is Asked
Designing an incident response plan with region-aware routing and safe rollback demonstrates depth in observability design and production reliability.

## Key Concepts
- Observability and signal fusion
- Region-based SLOs and traffic shaping
- Circuit breakers and fallback paths
- Canary and synthetic testing at the edge

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo per-region circuit breaker sketch
const breakers = new Map();
function allowed(region){
  const b = breakers.get(region) ?? {open:false, since:0, failures:0};
  return !b.open;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle compliance and data sovereignty in this plan?
- How would you validate rollback safety under real traffic with limited data?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesss real-world ability to design resilient, low-tail-latency multi-region pipelines under stress while preserving tenant fairness and clear rollback paths.

## Key Concepts

- Backpressure and circuit breaking in streaming pipelines
- Per-tenant QoS and traffic shaping
- Exactly-once processing guarantees across Kafka and sinks
- Observability for SLO-driven tail latency
- Chaos testing and incident rollback discipline

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: bounded per-tenant backpressure
function handleEvent(event, tenant) {
  const q = queues[tenant];
  if (q.length < MAX_PER_TENANT) {
    enqueue(event, tenant);
  } else {
    drop(event); // apply backpressure upstream
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the degradation plan with synthetic workloads?
- What metrics would you use to decide when to restore normal traffic?

